# Target Makefile fragment for Symphony/Dynphony.
#
# No hardware multiply/divide (docs/isa.txt) and no mulsi3/divsi3/etc.
# patterns are defined in symphony.md, so GCC automatically synthesizes
# calls to libgcc2.c's portable __mulsi3/__udivsi3/__divsi3/__umodsi3/
# __modsi3 (and the 64-bit __muldi3 etc., built from the 32-bit ones).
# Nothing extra needs to be listed here for that -- it is libgcc's
# default behavior whenever a target's .md leaves those RTL patterns
# undefined.
#
# No hardware floating point either, but this ABI does not use float/
# double in the freestanding runtime, so no soft-float libgcc pieces
# are pulled in beyond what libgcc2.c already provides unconditionally.

# One ABI, one instruction-selection strategy for both encodings
# (Symphony vs Dynphony differs only in final byte width, handled
# entirely by the downstream assembler -- see symphony.opt). No
# multilib variants needed.
MULTILIB_OPTIONS =
MULTILIB_DIRNAMES =
